"08_number_parse.mst — `Number class >> fromString:` (DolphinDart DD10).

 Dolphin's type converters parse the view side through it: `NumberToText`'s
 `rightToLeft:` is `Number fromString: aString`, and that is the call the DD10
 bad-input path turns into an `InvalidFormat`.

 **It RAISES on unparseable input.** The world's `String>>asInteger` answers
 nil, which is the right contract for a query but the wrong one here: a
 converter that answers nil on garbage puts nil into the model, and the failure
 then surfaces wherever that nil is next used — arbitrarily far from the field
 the user typed in. Raising is what lets the presenter beep and revert at the
 point of the mistake.

 `InvalidFormat` (st/dolphin_compat/03_kernel.mst, on DD4's `Error`) is the
 class Dolphin signals, so `on: InvalidFormat do:` in translated code catches
 it and so does any existing `on: Error do:`."
Object subclass: Number [
    Number class >> fromString: aString [
        ^self fromString: aString ifInvalid: [
            InvalidFormat new signal: '''', aString displayString,
                ''' is not a valid number' ]
    ]

    "The non-raising form, for a caller that has somewhere better to put the
     failure. Integers first, then a single decimal point — the two forms the
     corpus's converters accept."
    Number class >> fromString: aString ifInvalid: aBlock [
        | s dot whole frac sign body |
        s := aString displayString.
        s isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^aBlock value ].
        sign := 1. body := s.
        (body at: 1) = $- ifTrue: [ sign := -1. body := body copyFrom: 2 to: body size ].
        (body at: 1) = $+ ifTrue: [ body := body copyFrom: 2 to: body size ].
        body isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^aBlock value ].
        dot := 0.
        1 to: body size do: [ :i | (body at: i) = $. ifTrue: [ dot := i ] ].
        dot = 0 ifTrue: [
            whole := body asInteger.
            whole isNil ifTrue: [ ^aBlock value ].
            ^whole * sign ].
        "A decimal point at either end, or more than one, is not a number."
        (dot = 1 or: [ dot = body size ]) ifTrue: [ ^aBlock value ].
        whole := (body copyFrom: 1 to: dot - 1) asInteger.
        frac := (body copyFrom: dot + 1 to: body size).
        (whole isNil or: [ frac asInteger isNil ]) ifTrue: [ ^aBlock value ].
        ^sign * (whole + (frac asInteger / (10 raisedTo: frac size))) asFloat
    ]
]
